  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mr.Shathishkumar Dahyal Patel vs Food Safety Officer on 13 March, 2023 Author: G.Ilangovan Bench: G.Ilangovan Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Date of Reservation : 13/03/2023 Date of Pronouncement : 14/08/2023 Coram: The Hon'Ble Mr Justice G.Ilangovan Crl.OP(MD)No.2417 of 2023 and Crl.MP(MD)No.2175 of 2023 1.Mr",
    "facts": "This criminal original petition has been filed seeking quashment of the case in CC No776 of 2019 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.1, Madurai. 2.The case of the prosecution in brief:- The complainant namely the Food Safety Officer attached to Madurai Corporation, Viswanathapuram filed a private complaint stating that on information on 17/09/2018 at about 11.30 am along with police team, he made search in Door No.17, Othuvar Lane, Keela Chithrai Veethi, Madurai. At that time the shop owner by name Barvin V.Jail was available. They introduced themselves to the shop owner and made search with the consent of the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis shop owner. At that time, they found the following banned tobacco products:- Ganesh 701 Tobacco Premium Product 28 pockets Ganesh 701 Tobacco Premium 21 pocket Shankar Chaap Tobacco 6 pockets Miraj Swadeshi Tobacco 25 pockets RMD PANMASALA 50 boxes M Scented Tobacco Gold 56 boxes 3.Samples were lifted as per the procedure. Further process was undertaken as per the procedure and rules. The shop owner was also informed about the sending of samples to the laboratory for examination. Samples were sent to the laboratory by following proper procedure and rules. A report was received from forensic analysis, on 29/11/2018. In the above said report, it has been stated that it was unsafe under sections 3(1)(zz)(iii) & (V), 26(2)(i) & (V) of Food Safety and Standards Act and also the sale of chewable tobacco is Prohibited as per the Tamil Nadu Government Gazzette No.184, Mr.Shathishkumar Dahyal Patel vs Food Safety Officer on 13 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/191067817/ 2 dated 23/05/2018 and r/w section 26(2)(iv) of Food Safety and Standards Act 2006. After getting proper sanction order, he has filed a complaint on 15/07/2019. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 4.Seeking quashment of the same, this petition has been filed on the sole ground that the tobacco products banning order was challenged in Writ Appeal No.2093 of 2018 and WP Nos.3076 and 3084 of 2019. One of the writ petition No.3076 of 2019 was filed to quash the private complaint pending on the file of the Judicial Magistrate No.II, Ariyalur in CC No.129 of 2018 and another Writ Petition in WP No.3084 of 2019 was filed seeking quashment of the Government Order, vide Tamil Nadu Government Gazette Extraordinary No.184 (No. 1418/2013/S8/FSSA), dated 23.05.2018. 5.Heard both sides. 6.As mentioned above, this petition has been filed solely on the ground of order passed by the Division Bench of this court in WA No.2093 of 2018, dated 20/01/2023. The GO No.184 (No.1418/2013/S8/FSSA), dated 23.05.2018 was the subject matter of WP No.3076 of 2019. In the judgment reported in the case of The Designated Officer, The Food Safety & Drugs Control Department Vs. Jayavilas Tobacco (2023-1-L.W-639), elaborate discussion was made by the Division Bench of this court. 7.The above said writ petition was allowed by the single Judge. Challenging the same, Food Safety Officer filed writ appeal before the Division Bench, as mentioned above.",
    "arguments": "(v)Whether the provisions of Section 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 confer the power on the Commissioner, Food Safety to impose a total ban on the sale of Tobacco and Tobacco products by issuing successive notification year on year.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "(v)Whether the provisions of Section 30(2)(a) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 confer the power on the Commissioner, Food Safety to impose a total ban on the sale of Tobacco and Tobacco products by issuing successive notification year on year."
  },
